flowchart TB
    accTitle: How the weekly refresh of the lock files merges
    accDescr: On Mondays Renovate refreshes the lock files of every package manager. npm takes only versions released at least a week before. After Renovate, blueprint.py compiles the lock files of pip-compile again from uploads at least a week old, and keeps what main pins, such as the fix of a vulnerability. The check dependency-review asks PyPI and the registry of npm when each version that the refresh adds came out. Once every one is at least a week old and every check passes, the refresh merges on its own; a younger one holds it, and the check names it. The refresh of Composer and of any other package manager, which can't keep to that age, waits for the maintainer on a branch of its own.

    monday(["Renovate refreshes the lock files, on Mondays"])
    npm["npm: only versions<br>released a week before"]
    pip["pip-compile: blueprint.py compiles<br>them again from uploads a week<br>old, and keeps what main pins"]
    other["Composer and any other:<br>the newest versions"]
    age{"Is every version that the<br>refresh adds a week old?"}
    merge["Merges on its own<br>once every check passes"]
    held["Waits, and the check<br>names each younger one"]
    maintainer["Waits for the maintainer,<br>on renovate/review-…"]

    monday --> npm --> age
    monday --> pip --> age
    monday --> other --> maintainer
    age -- "yes" --> merge
    age -- "no" --> held

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class monday,npm,pip,other,age bot
    class held,maintainer person
    class merge done
